Micro Magic's MegaCell Compiler (MMI_MC2.0).

The Micro Magic MegaCell Compiler (MCC) builds large regular/array
structures based on an algorithmic description of the cell relative
positions.  This feature is sometimes referred to as "tiling".  In
addition, the arrays can be programmed, netlisted, and a critical path
extracted from the finished structure.

The MegaCell Compiler relies on Micro Magic's MAX to store and
manipulate the underlying data layout data structures.


INSTALLATION

To install the MegaCell Compiler, you must add the line 

	mc_init

to your .maxrc file, typically the one in
${MMI_TOOLS}/../mmi_local/max/.maxrc.  You also need a special license
(max_mcc) to run MCC.
